A command analysed for linux and windows. A directive sits in a file only the
windows configuration compiles, and another in a file both compile. Each binds
its unreferenced function and is in effect, and the shared file's directive is
one record whichever configurations read it.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}, "analysis": {"configurations": [
  {"id": "linux-amd64", "os": "linux", "arch": "amd64"},
  {"id": "windows-amd64", "os": "windows", "arch": "amd64"}]}}
-- main.go --
package main

func main() {}

//deadset:ignore DS1002 -- kept for every platform
func shared() {}
-- extra_windows.go --
package main

//deadset:ignore DS1002 -- kept for the windows loader
func windowsOnly() {}
